For an early-game stash, the level with the entrance to the mines can
be a good place, since it'll be the topmost level you'll be frequently
going through.  As others said, bottom of Sokoban is good of course,
as is Minetown -- but so is any other level with an altar.  On levels
with shops, I sometimes keep my stash _in_ the shop; it makes for easy
price ID'ing, and you can use the shopkeeper as a doorman by picking
up an unpaid junk item.  Don't try this if you have teleportitis, of
course (or make sure you have credit).

Until you get a BoH and/or easy levelporting, you'll be leaving little
piles every second level or so anyway.  Just keep track of what's in
each pile, and make sure your notes are up to date!  Nothing sucks
like running back to a food stash hungry only to find that you already
ate it all the last time you were there.

It's also useful to think about 1) how soon you may be needing each
item, 2) how urgent will it be when you do need it, and 3) where will
you most likely be needing it.

